#: ../../../install_mamba.rst:5
msgid "Mamba Install Xonsh"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_mamba.rst:7
msgid ""
"Xonsh is a Python-based shell, and running xonsh requires Python to be "
"installed. The Python version and its packages can be installed in various "
"locations. When you execute ``import`` or any other Python code during a "
"xonsh session, it is executed in the Python environment that was used to "
"start the current xonsh instance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_mamba.rst:13
msgid ""
"When xonsh is used as a core shell, it is necessary to keep the Python "
"environment with xonsh stable, predictable, and independent of system "
"changes. Lightweight environment managers such as ``venv``, ``pipx``, or "
"``rye`` do not fully address this requirement. Package managers that can "
"install fully isolated Python environments as a core feature, such as "
"``miniconda`` or ``micromamba``, should be used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_mamba.rst:20
msgid ""
"The ``mamba-install-xonsh.sh`` script creates an independent Python "
"environment for xonsh using `mamba <https://mamba.readthedocs.io/>`_ in "
"``$TARGET_DIR`` without affecting any other components of the system. This "
"is an isolated, xonsh-specific environment that is not affected by system "
"package upgrades, Python version changes, or other experiments with "
"environments. You can use ``xpip`` and ``xmamba`` to intentionally install "
"packages into this environment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_mamba.rst:27
msgid "Install the latest xonsh release with a well-tested Python version:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_mamba.rst:29
msgid ""
"$ TARGET_DIR=$HOME/.local/xonsh-env PYTHON_VER=3.11 XONSH_VER='xonsh[full]' "
"\\\n"
"  /bin/bash -c \"$(curl -fsSL https://xon.sh/install/mamba-install-xonsh."
"sh)\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_mamba.rst:34
msgid "Install xonsh from the ``main`` Git branch with a stable Python version"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_mamba.rst:36
msgid ""
"$ TARGET_DIR=$HOME/.local/xonsh-env PYTHON_VER=3.11 XONSH_VER='xonsh[full] @ "
"git+https://github.com/xonsh/xonsh@main' \\\n"
"  /bin/bash -c \"$(curl -fsSL https://xon.sh/install/mamba-install-xonsh."
"sh)\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_mamba.rst:42
msgid "Preinstall and preload `xontribs <https://github.com/topics/xontrib>`_:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_mamba.rst:44
msgid ""
"$ TARGET_DIR=$HOME/.local/xonsh-env PYTHON_VER=3.11 XONSH_VER='xonsh[full] @ "
"git+https://github.com/xonsh/xonsh@main' \\\n"
"  PIP_INSTALL=\"uv xontrib-sh xontrib-jump-to-dir xontrib-dalias xontrib-"
"pipeliner xontrib-whole-word-jumping\" \\\n"
"  XONSHRC=\"\\$XONSH_HISTORY_BACKEND = 'sqlite'; xontrib load -s sh "
"jump_to_dir pipeliner whole_word_jumping dalias; \\$PROMPT = \\$PROMPT."
"replace('{prompt_end}', '\\n{prompt_end}')\" \\\n"
"  /bin/bash -c \"$(curl -fsSL https://xon.sh/install/mamba-install-xonsh."
"sh)\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_mamba.rst:52
msgid "Usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_mamba.rst:54
msgid ""
"After installation, you no longer need to worry about Python or package "
"manipulations unintentionally breaking the shell. You can safely use "
"``pip``, ``brew``, and other package managers without corrupting the xonsh "
"environment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_mamba.rst:58
msgid "After installation:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_mamba.rst:60
msgid "``xonsh`` refers to ``~/.local/xonsh-env/xbin/xonsh``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_mamba.rst:61
msgid "``xpython`` refers to ``~/.local/xonsh-env/bin/python``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_mamba.rst:62
msgid "``xpip`` refers to ``~/.local/xonsh-env/bin/python -m pip``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_mamba.rst:63
msgid "``xcontext`` shows the current context."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_mamba.rst:64
msgid "You can run ``source xmamba.xsh`` to activate mamba (see below)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_mamba.rst:66
msgid "Additions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_mamba.rst:68
msgid ""
"``xbin-xonsh`` runs xonsh from xonsh-env if ``xonsh`` is overridden in "
"``$PATH``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_mamba.rst:69
msgid "``xbin-python`` runs Python from xonsh-env."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_mamba.rst:70
msgid "Executable helpers from xonsh-env:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_mamba.rst:72
msgid ""
"``xbin-hidden`` lists the internal hidden ``bin`` directory of xonsh-env. "
"Example: ``xpip install lolcat && xbin-hidden``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_mamba.rst:74
msgid ""
"``xbin-add`` adds an executable from the hidden ``bin`` directory to the "
"visible ``xbin``. Example: ``xbin-add lolcat``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_mamba.rst:76
msgid "``xbin-list`` lists executables in the visible ``xbin`` directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_mamba.rst:77
msgid ""
"``xbin-del`` removes an executable from ``xbin``. The executable remains in "
"``bin``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_mamba.rst:81
msgid "Tips and Tricks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_mamba.rst:84
msgid "Using mamba from xonsh-env"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_mamba.rst:86
msgid "To bind the xonsh-env micromamba to the ``xmamba`` alias, run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_mamba.rst:88
msgid "@ source xmamba.xsh"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_mamba.rst:92
msgid "You can then use:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_mamba.rst:94
msgid ""
"@ xmamba activate base  # Environment where xonsh was installed.\n"
"@ pip install lolcat    # Install ``lolcat`` into the ``base`` environment.\n"
"@ xmamba deactivate\n"
"\n"
"@ xmamba create --name myenv python=3.12\n"
"@ xmamba activate myenv\n"
"@ pip install lolcat    # Install ``lolcat`` into ``myenv``.\n"
"@ xmamba deactivate"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_mamba.rst:106
msgid "Cleaning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_mamba.rst:108
msgid ""
"If you do not plan to use ``xmamba``, you can reclaim disk space using "
"`mamba clean <https://fig.io/manual/mamba/clean>`_:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_mamba.rst:111
msgid ""
"@ source xmamba.xsh\n"
"@ xmamba clean -a"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_mamba.rst:117
msgid "Uninstall"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_mamba.rst:119
msgid "Simply delete ``$TARGET_DIR``. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_mamba.rst:121
msgid "@ rm -rf ~/.local/xonsh-env/"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_mamba.rst:126
msgid "Known Issues"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_mamba.rst:129
msgid "Do not blindly use as a login shell"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_mamba.rst:131
msgid ""
"Using xonsh as a `login shell <https://linuxhandbook.com/login-shell/>`_ is "
"not recommended unless you are experienced and understand the implications. "
"Many tools expect the login shell to be POSIX-compliant, and issues may "
"arise when such tools attempt to run POSIX-specific commands in xonsh."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_mamba.rst:137
msgid "``std::bad_alloc``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_mamba.rst:139
msgid "If you encounter the error::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_mamba.rst:141
msgid "terminate called after throwing an instance of 'std::bad_alloc'"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_mamba.rst:143
msgid ""
"delete the target directory (for example, ``rm -rf ~/.local/xonsh-env/``) "
"and repeat the installation."
msgstr ""
